ads, 16 Sep (leadership-account): Subject: Tiled Canvas. 'The numbers could not be clearer: people with Tiled Canvas crash nearly three times as often as everyone else, and the overall rate climbed step for step with the ramp. I don't need another week of analysis. The plan is to turn the flag off for everyone on Thursday, mark the crash incident resolved, and let 7.4.0 go to 100% on Friday as scheduled. The canvas team can bring the feature back when they can prove it is stable.'\n- Internal release notes, Quillmark Android 7.4.0 (change-record): Staged rollout through the app store: offered to 5% of users on 2 Sep and 25% on 6 Sep; 100% planned for 18 Sep. The store offers the update to a random share of users, who then install it at their own pace. Everyone else stays on 7.3.2. Changes in 7.4.0: (1) Tiled Canvas client code, which stays inactive unless the tiled_canvas flag is on; (2) image library Pixelda upgraded from 2.8 to 3.1 to support HEIF photo attachments; (3) Tracewell crash-reporting SDK upgraded from 4.9 to 5.0, which adds capture of native (C/C++) crashes; (4) notification channel cleanup; (5) translation updates.\n- Flag service configuration export, tiled_canvas, 16 Sep (system-record): flag: tiled_canvas | owner: canvas-team | eligibility: client must report capability canvas.tiles.v1 (comment: 'capability first shipped in 7.4.0; not present in 7.3.x') | bucketing: random by hashed user id | rollout history: 4 Sep 10% of eligible users; 7 Sep 50%; 10 Sep 90% | holdout: the remaining 10% of eligible users stay off | kill switch: available, takes effect at next app start.\n- Incident channel #inc-crash-rate, excerpt, 15 Sep (staff-account): Dev (SRE): 'sync-service deployed on 9 Sep around 14:00 UTC, and the overall crash curve gets steeper around then. Might not be the client at all.' Priya (canvas engineer): 'Tiled Canvas holds more texture memory than the old canvas. If anything is ours, it will be on low-RAM phones.' Tomás (PM): 'Also remember who ends up with the flag in practice. Our heaviest sketchers update first, and heavy users always crash more.' Nobody in the thread posted figures broken down by app version, device or usage.\n\nBRIEF:\nThe crash gap is mostly not caused by Tiled Canvas. Only 7.4.0 users can have the flag, so the flag group is simply the 7.4.0 group. Build 7.4.0 crashed at about 2% from its first days (2–3 Sep), before the flag ramp began, while 7.3.2 stayed at about 0.7%. Among 7.4.0 users, flag-on is 2.10% and the random flag-off holdout is 1.98%, a difference that could be noise. The biggest crash cluster is a native crash in the upgraded image library (Pixelda, HEIF decoding), and it doesn't appear in 7.3.2. No crash stacks involve the canvas code. The app-store console, which is independent of the crash SDK, shows the same gap, so it isn't a reporting artifact. Device mix and usage are about the same across groups. The 9 Sep sync-service deploy didn't move 7.3.2 rates. A small flag effect of a few tenths of a point can't be ruled out. Do not turn the flag off and declare it resolved, and do not take 7.4.0 to 100%. Hold the rollout at 25%, fix the Pixelda crash, and keep the existing holdout running (widening it would speed up the flag measurement). Don't roll back the crash SDK, since that would hide crashes. Confidence is fairly high.\n","numLines":19,"startLine":1,"totalLines":19}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UfgD6FGtEb47c2hpwvbSUL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
